[OPTION - Scan Windows STARTUP Programs]
{\rtf1\ansi\fs22
This Option scans all Windows STARTUP locations on \b this machine \b0 and builds a complete list of every program, 
helper, updater, scheduler, and background component that runs when Windows starts. \par
\par
Many systems accumulate \b far too many \b0 startup items over time.  These can slow down boot time, reduce performance, 
and make Windows feel sluggish.  Because every PC is different, the STARTUP list must be scanned \b on each machine \b0 
to identify what is actually present. \par
\par
The PRO Version consults On2it Software's online Knowledge Base to obtain \b clear, plain‑English Advice \b0 for each item it finds.  
This includes: \par
\b   •  \b0What the program does, \par
\b   •  \b0Whether it is essential or optional, \par
\b   •  \b0Whether it is safe to disable, \par
\b   •  \b0Whether it is known to cause slowdowns, \par
\b   •  \b0Whether it is associated with OEM bloat, trialware, or background updaters. \par
\par
If an item is \b not yet \b0 in the Knowledge Base, it uses AI to generate new Advice automatically.  
These new entries are \b reviewed manually from time to time \b0 to ensure the Advice remains accurate and appropriate. \par
\par
This scan appends a new Group, with Options, and Advice to the bottom of the left-hand panel, based on what it finds on your machine.  
So that you can make informed decisions about what YOU want to run at startup. \par
}


