[OPTION - Use Options SAVED previously]
{\rtf1\ansi\fs22
This Option loads a previously SAVED set of Groups and Options created on this or another machine.  
These saved selections allow you to reuse a known‑good configuration without having to re‑select everything manually. \par
\par
Saved Option Sets are especially useful when you maintain multiple PCs, or when you want to apply the same decisions 
across several machines.  They preserve your earlier choices, including which STARTUP items you disabled and which 
INSTALLED Programs you removed or kept. \par
\par
Because every machine is different, some saved Options may not apply to the current system.  
When this happens, the PRO Version keeps your saved selections but simply ignores any items that do not exist on this machine.  
Nothing is lost, and nothing is overwritten. \par
\par
Using 'SAVED Options' reapplies your previous choices to any matching Groups and Options already shown in the left‑hand panel.  
Including a Windows Activation Key, if one was saved earlier (encrypted if a Password was specified). \par
}

[OPTION - Enable Activations]
{\rtf1\ansi\fs22
When selected without a set of previously saved Options specified, 
a Dialog Box will be displayed at the start of a 'PERFORM Selected Operations' run, 
which enables you to specify the:  \par
\b    •   Activation Key,\b0 \par
\b    •   Encryption Password.\b0 \par
These enable the same Windows Activation ID to be used to activate multiple PCs using the same 'SAVED Options' Set.  \par
\par
If Activation is Enabled a Key MUST be specified or the run will not proceed. \par
\par 
If an Encryption Password is specified the Activation Key will be encrypted with the Password when the Options are saved.  
If NO Password is specified the Activation Key will NOT be encrypted.  \par
\par
When Activation is attempted using a set of 'SAVED Options', the User will be prompted for the Password (if one was specified) 
so that the Activation Key can be decrypted.  \par
}


