[OPTION - Remove OneDrive]
{\rtf1\ansi\fs22
OneDrive is Microsoft's 'Cloud' Service that will automatically replicate your files to their servers on the Internet.  
They will \b try \b0 to convince you that it is an automatic backup - \b it is NOT! \b0   
Any mistakes you make in your copy will be replicated to their copy.  
If you accidentally delete your copy, their copy gets deleted too.\par
\par
OneDrive is useful if you want more than one device and/or user to have access to the same file.  
But even then, you still need a good backup system that keeps multiple versions offline - 
to protect you from accidental file deletions and unwanted changes.  \par
\par
Microsoft will store your files for free up to 5 GB; beyond that they will charge you.  
OneDrive is also very intrusive on your day-to-day operations, stealing files and hiding them in the cloud.  
For most users, OneDrive causes more confusion than benefit.  \par
\par
A true backup keeps multiple historical versions stored offline, where they cannot be changed by accident.  
If you want a good backup that keeps your files on a separate device, 
then we strongly recommend that you investigate third party backup tools such as 'EaseUS ToDo Backup', 
or many other FREE backup applications. \par
\par 
Other cloud services such as DropBox and Google Drive are also worth you considering, as an alternative to OneDrive.
}

