[OPTION - KEEP Recall]
{\rtf1\ansi\fs22
\b One of the biggest frustrations when using a computer is finding something interesting
 - only to forget where you saw it. \b0  Microsoft intend to solve this problem with Windows Recall.  \par
Recall automatically captures snapshots of your screen at periodic intervals.  \par
\par
When it was first announced many users expressed concern about potential privacy problems.  
Microsoft withdrew the product and addressed these concerns, by ensuring all data is 
\b encrypted \b0 and \b stored locally\b0 .  
So, no data is uploaded to the cloud.  \par
\par
Recall enables users to search and interact with previous content using natural language queries, 
enhancing productivity and memory recall.\par
\par
Think of Recall as a visual AI-searchable Browser History.  But instead of tracking only web activity, 
Recall extends to everything you do on your PC, making it easier to find and re-engage with past content.\par
\par
It is exclusive to the latest so-called AI PCs, equipped with an NPU (Neural Processing Unit).  
It is now disabled by default, and users must actively enable it themselves.\par
\par
So, if you are lucky enough to have it on your PC; keep it, try it.  
If in the end you don't like it, disable it.\par
}
